<ansi fg="black-bold">.:</ansi> <ansi fg="magenta">Help for </ansi><ansi fg="command">rake</ansi>

The <ansi fg="command">rake</ansi> command drives your natural claws across your opponent,
tearing open wounds that continue to bleed. It deals moderate
damage and applies a bleeding condition on a successful strike.

<ansi fg="yellow">Requirements:</ansi>

  - Must have natural claws (clawed species only)
  - Must be in active combat
  - Cannot be used if special move cooldown is active

<ansi fg="yellow">Usage:</ansi>

  <ansi fg="command">rake</ansi>
  Attempt to rake your current combat target

<ansi fg="yellow">Mechanics:</ansi>

  <ansi fg="stat">Damage:</ansi> Moderate — the slashing strike itself deals real harm.
  <ansi fg="stat">Bleed:</ansi> A successful rake opens wounds that continue to
    bleed over several rounds, dealing additional damage beyond
    the initial strike.
  <ansi fg="stat">Cooldown:</ansi> Shared with other special moves.
  <ansi fg="stat">Skill:</ansi> Progresses Unarmed Combat

Rake's persistent bleed makes it valuable for wearing down
opponents over the course of a longer fight. See
<ansi fg="command">help conditions</ansi> for details on the bleeding effect.

<ansi fg="yellow">See Also:</ansi>

  <ansi fg="command">help hamstring</ansi>, <ansi fg="command">help kick</ansi>,
  <ansi fg="command">help conditions</ansi>, <ansi fg="command">help combat</ansi>
